<title>ECUADOR: Former Ecuador energy min to head state oil firm.</title>
<headline>Former Ecuador energy min to head state oil firm.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Former Ecuadorean Energy Minister Rafael Almeida will be appointed president of state-run oil company Petroecuador, Energy Minister Raul Baca said Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;The country's oil situation will be explained in coming days once Rafael Ameida is named president of Petroecuador,&quot; Baca told reporters.</p>
<p>Almeida was energy minister from 1988 to 1992.</p>
<p>((-Maria Veronica Barreiros, Quito newsroom, 5932 258433))</p>
